From: plotarmordev <299844489+plotarmordev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:33:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 03/18] nemotron: a decode window's latent shared-expert plans
 are built once, at buffer load, one per row count

The shared expert's pairs are the same (row, share) list at every layer, so initShared now plans each row count up to
max_rows into its own slice of the shared buffer and the expert pass reuses it instead of planning per layer. Prompt
passes wider than a window and remote rank jobs still plan for their row count. A host test checks that the row
counts' plans never overlap at one share or two.

A prompt segment's buffers (Buffers.sibling) take the owner's shared plans and pair ids instead of scratch of their
own, since only the owner's load writes them. In 1.0.12 each segment had pair ids of its own that nothing wrote, so a
segmented Super prompt planned its shared expert from uninitialised memory.
